    "one_liner": "Tipperary is a crowdsourced mobile app that shows diners the average tip size at any restaurant, removing the guesswork and anxiety from one of dining's most awkward moments.",
    "sections": {
      "1_problem": {
        "headline": "Tipping is broken, opaque, and stressful.",
        "pain_points": [
          "Diners have no reliable reference point for what is 'normal' at a given restaurant, so they either overtip out of guilt or undertip out of ignorance.",
          "Tipping norms vary wildly by city, cuisine, service style (counter vs. full service), and price tier, yet every diner is left to guess.",
          "Servers suffer from inconsistent income because tipping is driven by social pressure rather than shared expectations.",
          "Travelers and newcomers face cultural confusion, often tipping incorrectly and feeling embarrassed.",
          "Digital checkout screens now prompt tips everywhere (coffee shops, food trucks, takeout), amplifying 'tip fatigue' and confusion."
        ],
        "market_signal": "Over 70% of U.S. diners report feeling anxious or uncertain about how much to tip, and 'tipflation' has become a mainstream media topic."
      },
      "2_solution": {
        "headline": "A real-time, location-aware tipping benchmark for every restaurant.",
        "description": "Tipperary aggregates anonymized, crowdsourced tip data and displays the average tip percentage and dollar amount for each restaurant, broken down by meal type, party size, and service format.",
        "how_it_works": [
          "Open the app or scan the receipt at the end of a meal.",
          "Tipperary auto-detects the restaurant via GPS or receipt scan.",
          "The app shows the venue's average tip, the local norm, and a suggested range.",
          "The user logs their tip in one tap (optional), enriching the dataset.",
          "The user earns reputation points and unlocks insights for contributing."
        ]
      },
      "3_product": {
        "core_features": [
          {
            "name": "Tip Benchmark",
            "detail": "Average tip percentage and amount per restaurant, with confidence indicators based on sample size."
